# Demo Mode: Skip Type Checks & Linting

This project is currently in **demo mode**. The priority is a working, visually
correct, click-through demo — not type safety or lint cleanliness.

- Do NOT run `tsc`, `next build` type-check, `npm run lint`, or similar
  verification commands after making changes, unless the user explicitly
  asks for one.
- Do NOT block on, fix, or report TypeScript/ESLint errors unless they
  actually break the running demo (e.g. a runtime crash).
- It's fine to use quick-and-dirty types (`any`, `as`, `@ts-ignore`, loose
  props) to keep moving — don't spend time refining types.
- After finishing an implementation task, **stop**. Do not verify, smoke-test,
  or "confirm" anything unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do NOT start, restart, or kill the dev server (`npm run dev`, `next dev`, etc.)
  unless the user explicitly asks — assume one is already running and leave it.
- Do NOT curl/fetch pages, open browsers, or poll terminals to check that the
  app renders. Hot reload will pick up changes; the user will look when ready.
- Skip the entire post-task verification step: no type checks, no lint, no
  render checks, no dev-server status checks.
- `next.config.ts` has `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors` and
  `eslint.ignoreDuringBuilds` set to `true` so `next build`/`next dev` won't
  fail on type or lint errors. Keep these settings unless the user asks to
  re-enable strict checks.
